# Shell scripts must keep LF. core.autocrlf=true was rewriting them to CRLF on checkout, and
# a Linux bash then fails on the \r: "set: -: invalid option", "syntax error near unexpected
# token $'in\r'". Harmless while every runner executed under Git Bash on Windows; fatal the
# moment one is uploaded to a Linux container (Modal, or any rented GPU box).
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else executed by a shell or read line-by-line remotely.
*.jinja text eol=lf
